{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:350b9ef5291759a0","name":"M22-T Krayt Gunship","source":{"id":"source:reference-350b9ef5291759a0","title":"M22-T Krayt Gunship","revision":20699,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:21:15Z","sha256":"e94d896baefe41262737bf6b8808c19a0e5da969d9c80c455292e10869b65f1e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20699","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=M22-T%20Krayt%20Gunship&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-350b9ef5291759a0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Hutt Kajidics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Hutt_Kajidics","referenceId":"reference:3f107406b356c3df"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The M22-T \"Krayt\" Gunship was originally commissioned by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jabba the Hutt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jabba_the_Hutt","referenceId":"reference:4f1583c9ec5e6852"}," to serve as a command ship for his most powerful and loyal lieutenants. The design proved successful and popular, and MandalMotors produced many more such gunships, but only as special orders for valued clients. It was the last of the \"Scaled Killer\" series (including the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dunelizard Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dunelizard_Fighter"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["M12-L Kimogila"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/M12-L_Kimogila?action=edit&redlink=1"},", and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scyk Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scyk_Fighter"},"), and it was so heavily armed and armored that it finally drew the Empire's attention to MandalMotors' independent military constructions. The Imperial advisor who allowed its design and sale was imprisoned, and various Imperial sycophants took his place for several years. After the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endor"},", MandalMotors workers ousted the Imperial advisor's position in favor of supporting ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because of its origin as a specially ordered craft, the M22-T Krayt Gunship has a few unusual features. First, it has numerous cover panels that have little purpose but aesthetics, which can be modified or removed to suit the tastes of each owner. Second, the ship has room for two passengers (or prisoners), which allows it to be used as an armed shuttle or a prisoner transport as well as an attack craft.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The \"Krayt\" carries four ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"}," under the pilot's control, a Gunner's turret that can be armed with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Cannons"},", and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missile Launcher"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missile_Launcher"}," controlled by either the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"},". The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," has a clear field of fire and a dedicated targeting computer, which grants a +1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus to attack rolls with turret weapons (but not with the ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"},"). This heavy firepower makes the \"Krayt\" a highly effective attack craft, but it is too expensive for mass production. It remains most commonly found as a squad leader's fighter, a bounty hunter's personal vessel, or an escort for the wealthy.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["M22-T Krayt Gunship Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 28; +8 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 160; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"h